---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'August 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms for using UtilityBox's free calculators and tools, including the accuracy disclaimer for financial and technical tools."
>
  <div class="container terms-page">
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <section>
      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p>
        These terms cover your use of UtilityBox (this website). By using the site, you agree to them. If you
        don't agree, please don't use the site — there's no account or sign-up, so that's genuinely as simple
        as closing the tab.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The service</h2>
      <p>
        UtilityBox provides free calculators and utility tools that run in your browser — no account, no
        sign-up, no payment. We can change, add, remove, or discontinue any tool at any time, without notice.
        We try not to break things, but we don't promise the site or any specific tool will always be
        available, error-free, or uninterrupted.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>No professional advice — accuracy isn't guaranteed</h2>
      <p>
        This is the important one. Every tool on this site — including the UK Salary, VAT, Loan Repayment, Tip,
        and Percentage calculators, and the Network/CIDR calculator — is provided for general informational
        purposes only. None of it is financial, tax, legal, or professional advice, and none of it should be
        relied on as the sole basis for a financial, business, or technical decision.
      </p>
      <p>
        We've tried to implement the underlying formulas correctly and verified them against known reference
        figures, but tax rules, exchange rates, and interest calculations change, edge cases exist, and
        software has bugs. Always double-check anything that actually matters — a mortgage decision, a tax
        return, a production network configuration — with an authoritative source (HMRC, a qualified
        accountant or financial adviser, your bank, official documentation) before acting on it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>No warranty, no liability</h2>
      <p>
        The site and its tools are provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties of any kind, express
        or implied — including, without limitation, warranties of accuracy, merchantability, or fitness for a
        particular purpose.
      </p>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, we aren't liable for any loss or damage arising from your use
        of, or inability to use, this site or any tool on it — including decisions made or actions taken based
        on a tool's output. If you're a consumer in the UK, nothing in these terms excludes or limits liability
        where it would be unlawful to do so.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>Please don't:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Try to disrupt, overload, or interfere with the site (e.g. automated scraping at a rate that affects other visitors).</li>
        <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to any part of the site's infrastructure.</li>
        <li>Use the site for anything unlawful.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We reserve the right to block access for anyone who doesn't follow this.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        Some tools call out to third-party services to work — for example, the Currency Converter uses the
        Frankfurter API, and the site shows ads served by Google AdSense. Those services have their own terms
        and privacy practices, which we don't control. See our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for the
        full detail on what talks to what.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Content and word lists</h2>
      <p>
        The site's code and design are ours. The word list used by the Word Unscrambler and Word Builder tools
        incorporates the UK Advanced Cryptics Dictionary — see the credit at the bottom of those tool pages for
        the license it's used under.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms as the site changes. If we do, we'll update the "Last updated" date above.
        Continuing to use the site after a change means you accept the updated terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of England and Wales.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms? Email <strong>privacy@utilitybox.wales</strong>.</p>
      <p><a href="/">← Back to home</a></p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .terms-page {
    max-width: 720px;
    padding-block: var(--space-6) var(--space-8);
  }

  .updated {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  section h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  section ul {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  section p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  section li {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
</style>
